  "prompt": "I want a what-if shadow study for the Back Bay area of Boston, comparing today's buildings against a scenario where they are three times taller. The OSM extract is a file in this checkout at docs/examples/data/back_bay.osm.pbf. Load the buildings from it in the browser with Autark, and build two parallel branches that each accumulate shadow on the ground with a GPU shader over a solstice day: one using the real building heights and one using the raised heights, with the footprint-area criterion deciding which buildings get raised. Render each branch as its own 3D map so I can compare them side by side, and route both through a shared fan-out.",
